{
 "result": "csvsum.py is built and registered. It reads the whole stdin as bytes, splits on newlines, and for each row splits on commas with maxsplit 2 to get cat and val. Values are parsed as integer cents, with a fast path for the common two-decimal form, and sums are kept per cat. Output is sorted by cat with two decimals. It matches the sample out-0 byte for byte (cmp SAME, about 0.76s on 1M rows). The adopted variant (v0) measured +37% over the initial baseline (1.15346 to about 1.54, noise 4.1%). I am stopping here because the remaining gains look small against the cost of further trials.",
